Installed. Now let me check what @gravity-ui/uikit exports — I'll need ThemeProvider, TextInput, PasswordInput, Checkbox, Button. Let me verify the package version installed.

Gravity UI usage:
- Import styles: `@gravity-ui/uikit/styles/styles.css` (and fonts `@gravity-ui/uikit/styles/fonts.css`)
- ThemeProvider wrapper
- Components: TextInput, PasswordInput, Checkbox, Button, Card maybe

Let me write the App. In main.tsx or index.css import the gravity styles. Typically:

```ts
import '@gravity-ui/uikit/styles/fonts.css';
import '@gravity-ui/uikit/styles/styles.css';
```

Then App:

```tsx
import {Button, Checkbox, PasswordInput, TextInput, ThemeProvider} from '@gravity-ui/uikit';
```

ThemeProvider needs theme="light" or "dark". Also need class on root element: `g-root g-root_theme_light`. ThemeProvider does that? Actually ThemeProvider sets the class on document.body by default (rootClassName handling). In Gravity UI, `<ThemeProvider theme="light">` will add `g-root g-root_theme_light` classes to the body by default (scoped). Yes, by default it applies to document body unless `scoped` prop.

Let me build the login page:

```tsx
import {useState} from 'react';
import {Button, Card, Checkbox, PasswordInput, Text, TextInput, ThemeProvider} from '@gravity-ui/uikit';

export function App() {
  const [email, setEmail] = useState('');
  const [password, setPassword] = useState('');
  const [remember, setRemember] = useState(false);

  const handleSubmit = (e: React.FormEvent) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    // ...
  };

  return (
    <ThemeProvider theme="light">
      <main className="page">
        <Card className="login-card" type="container" size="l">
          <form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>
            <Text variant="header-2">Вход</Text>
            <TextInput
              label="Email"
              type="email"
              value={email}
              onUpdate={setEmail}
              placeholder="you@example.com"
              size="l"
            />
            <PasswordInput
              label="Пароль"
              value={password}
              onUpdate={setPassword}
              placeholder="Введите пароль"
              size="l"
            />
            <Checkbox
              content="Запомнить меня"
              checked={remember}
              onUpdate={setRemember}
              size="l"
            />
            <Button view="action" size="l" type="submit" width="max">
              Войти
            </Button>
          </form>
        </Card>
      </main>
    </ThemeProvider>
  );
}
```

Checkbox's onUpdate — Checkbox has onChange? In Gravity UI, Checkbox has `onUpdate(checked: boolean)`? Let me check: TextInput has onUpdate(value: string). Checkbox — has onChange (React.ChangeEventHandler) and onUpdate? In newer versions of @gravity-ui/uikit, Checkbox supports onUpdate. Yes, Checkbox has onUpdate(checked). Button has width="max" prop. Card type="container".

Also styles import — should import in main.tsx before index.css so our overrides win. Also fonts.

